      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "stem": "You are the F2 doctor covering four medical wards overnight. At 02:00 you are on Ward 7 rewriting a drug chart that has run out of space. Within ten minutes you are bleeped three times.\n\nA nurse on Ward 9 tells you that Mrs Hale, 81, admitted two days ago with a urinary tract infection, now has a NEWS2 score of 7 with a blood pressure of 84/50. A nurse on Ward 5 asks you to verify the death of a patient who died peacefully on an end-of-life care plan an hour ago. Meanwhile, the nurse on Ward 7 tells you that a patient's son has just arrived and wants to speak to a doctor about his father's CT scan, which has not yet been reported.\n\nThe medical registrar is busy in the Emergency Department. There is a hospital-at-night coordinator on duty.",
