        "reasoning": "[D] is the best response because it achieves the goal, putting the patient back at the centre, at no cost to the relationship. [A] is a sensible escalation of the same aim. [E] is right in principle but likely to backfire. [B] and [C] are the weakest because each, in a different way, lets his own account fall away: [B] by dismissing his symptom and [C] by not listening to him at all.",
