          "brief": "A calm, private conversation is often the most effective and proportionate first challenge, even with a senior colleague.",
          "detailed": "Many people who behave like this have not recognised the effect on others, particularly in front of patients. Raising it one to one, by describing specific behaviour rather than labelling him, gives Mr Reid the chance to change without loss of face. It takes some courage as an F2, and his support for you makes it harder, not less necessary. If the conversation feels unsafe or does not help, the next step is [H]."
