        "keyDetails": "Chloe is 15 and asking for advice she can consent to herself if she is competent. Her partner is 16, which makes exploitation less likely, though not impossible. The pill is already being considered for her periods, so the clinical question is close to hand. Her mother is about to return.",
        "reasoning": "[C] determines whether Chloe can make this decision herself, [E] encourages family involvement while respecting her rights, and [H] carries out the safeguarding enquiry. Together they answer her question safely. The distractors either breach confidentiality ([A], [F]), withhold care ([B], [G]) or skip the safeguarding conversation ([D]).",
